SM-T715 tablet: the mobile data tile opens Réseau mobile.

A long press opens t715-mobile-settings (pkg/t715-modem), and so does a tap while
no connection exists, since the APN has to be set there first. Upstream's
"Mobile network" page (0.2.93, omamobile-sit) is the Pixel's; the tablet keeps
its own. Against omarchy-mobile 87b8395 (omamobile-shell 0.2.94) and the
patches before it, packages/omamobile-shell (applied with patch -p1 in that
directory; renumbered from 0007).

diff --git a/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/QuickSettings.qml b/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/QuickSettings.qml
index d4027cb..11b49ae 100644
--- a/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/QuickSettings.qml
+++ b/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/QuickSettings.qml
@@ -993,6 +993,9 @@ Item {
   // (omamobile-sit data on|off, which starts or stops
   // omamobile-sit-data.service through polkit). "No modem" until
   // omamobile-sitd publishes its state.
+  // SM-T715 tablet: NetworkManager's gsm connection, not omamobile-sit
+  // (0005), and a long press (or a tap with no connection) opens Réseau
+  // mobile (t715-mobile-settings), where the APN is set (0007).
   QtObject {
     id: mobileData
     readonly property bool available: root.probedHas("data")
@@ -1000,9 +1003,17 @@ Item {
     // Bars from the signal sitd reports; crossed out with no modem, data
     // off, or no network (TilesModel.dataIcon).
     readonly property string icon: TilesModel.dataIcon(available, enabled, root.probed.data_signal)
-    readonly property string status: !available ? "No modem"
+    readonly property string status: !available ? "Set up"
       : !enabled ? "Off" : (root.probed.data_status || "On")
-    function toggle() { if (available) root.runTileAction("mobile-data", !enabled) }
+    readonly property bool longPress: true
+    function toggle() {
+      if (available) root.runTileAction("mobile-data", !enabled)
+      else openDetails()
+    }
+    function openDetails() {
+      root.dismiss()
+      Quickshell.execDetached(["t715-mobile-settings"])
+    }
   }
 
   // Rotation lock over omamobile-autorotate (omamobile-sensors): it rotates
